'''Asturian''' (as-tū′ri-ạn), ''a.'' and ''n.'' [< Sp. ''Asturiano'', < ''Asturias'', Asturia, < L. ''Asturia'', the country of the Astures, in Hispania Tarraconensis, < ''Astur'', an Asturian. Cf. ''Astura'', a river in Asturia, now the ''Esla''.] '''I.''' ''a.'' Pertaining to ancient Asturia or modern Asturias, a northwestern province of Spain, on the bay of Biscay.

'''II.''' ''n.'' A native or an inhabitant of Asturia.

